# ------------------------------------------------------------------ puzzles

shot    maze
cap     A maze generator small enough to have won an obfuscated-C contest.
cap     It reads the number of rows on standard input and draws a maze that
cap     wide across the terminal.
try     echo 11 | maze
os9     echo 11 ! maze
run     echo 11 | maze
wait    8

shot    mines
cap     Minesweeper on a sixteen-by-sixteen board with forty mines.  Name a
cap     square by its row letter and then its column letter; answer the
cap     `Mark?' prompt with Y to flag it instead of opening it.  Opening a
cap     square clears everything around it that is safe and numbers the
cap     edges with how many mines they touch.  `q' quits.
try     mines
run     mines
wait    8
send    H\r
wait    3
send    H\r
wait    3
send    y\r
wait    5
snap
send    q
wait    2

shot    animal
cap     The guess-the-animal game, which learns: it asks yes-or-no questions
cap     down a tree of things it already knows and makes a final guess, and
cap     when it is wrong it asks you what you were thinking of and what
cap     question would have told the two apart, then writes the answer back
cap     into its data file.  A file to start from is in DOC/animal.
try     animal example
run     builtin cd /dd/DOC/animal
wait    1
run     clear
wait    1
run     animal example
wait    6
send    y\r
wait    3
send    y\r
wait    3
send    y\r
wait    3
send    y\r
wait    4
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    bog
cap     Boggle: sixteen lettered dice in a four-by-four tray and three
cap     minutes on the clock to type every word you can trace through
cap     adjoining letters.  `?' shows the rules.  Its word list, index and
cap     help text are in GAMES/BOG.
try     bog
run     bog
wait    8
send    \s
wait    6
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    hang
